WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.102
Ricardo, Nick,
congratulations.

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:04.937
You guys have made it
into the final round

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.372
of this competition.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.207
Now, we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:11.544
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.548
The ikakalaka.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:19.685
Heading off the weapon.

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:21.187
ARMORER: Weapon's hot.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:24.457
Today, we are
protesting the ikakalaka.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.593
So the ikakalaka is
a very unique sword.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.195
Looking at Dave's
weapon, I'm thinking,

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.697
oh, it's gonna be one of
those heavy weapons again.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:31.831
And I pick it up
and I'm like, no.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.165
It's not.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:34.934
You have a distal taper
that goes down there.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:37.670
So the weight is not at the tip.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.339
I was pleasantly surprised.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.475
Forged by the Mongo tribe
in the kingdom of Lunda

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:45.011
during the early 1800s,
the ikakalaka was

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.312
a fierce and imposing weapon.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.481
Designed for executions,
the double-edged blade

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.216
featured a thick spine
and large crescent

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:54.086
tip, giving it the ability
to forcibly chop with ease.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.189
This powerful weapon
with an ornate shape

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:58.090
quickly became
associated with wealth,

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:01.161
dignity, and social
position among men and women

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.528
in the Mongo tribe.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.465
The ikakalaka can be seen
in the 2018 blockbuster

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.833
film "Black Panther."

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:13.840
That crescent edge
acts like an ax head,

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.609
but you're thrusting
with the ax head.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.045
And then, you have the shaft, or
the length, of the blade there

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.246
that's double edge.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.449
Then, you can get
deep cuts with that.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:27.186
It's just like a sword, except
it's got a spatulated tip

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.755
that I can thrust with.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.527
When you pick up the
weapon and it works and it

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.729
functions the way
it was made to be,

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.598
it tells me a lot
about the smith.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.734
That means he not only
knows how to make it,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.736
he understands why he made it.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:47.373
That's bladesmithing.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.777
[blade whacking]

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:06.959
So having the crescent
head also gives

00:02:07.025 --> 00:02:09.595
you some curved edges to that.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.063
So one of the things
we're worried about

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:12.298
is you can get snagged.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.367
One, two, three, a point.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:17.703
So in wielding this, if I'm
gonna be slashing or chopping

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.907
something, I gotta make
sure that I use the shaft

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.107
and avoid the tip.

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:24.777
If I'm thrusting
with it, no problem.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:25.778
OK.

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:27.480
The whole weapon has to work.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.385
[squirts]

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:35.788
Good luck.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:36.890
We'll see you in four days.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.396
NICK HICKS: My
name is Nick Hicks.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.332 line:8%
What I like most
about bladesmithing

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.267 line:14%
is the artwork behind it.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.571
Being able to take
something most folks would

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.406
look at as a piece
of junk and turn it

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:57.843
into something beautiful
and usable, I think,

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.378
is the ultimate artwork.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:03.615 line:8%
I cut the 80c RV at an angle
to establish my scarf weld,

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:05.784 line:8%
so that when I stack
those billets up together,

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:10.189 line:8%
I'm going to try and mold those
down into the original blade

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:11.958
to make a crescent.
All right.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:13.225
Slowly but surely.

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:15.161
Plan is move a lot of steel.

00:03:15.227 --> 00:03:19.131
Get this thing shaped,
hopefully quenched.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.034
It's gonna be a
big, heavy blade.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.103
The weapon was made
as a serious chopper.

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:25.404
It will be heavy.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.774
But when you get
it in your hands,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.309
it will be a commanding tool.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:33.246
I'm gonna make sure our quench
tank is gonna accept this.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:36.415
Looks pretty good.

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:38.317
The time is definitely
an issue here.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.620
So I have to get
this thing quenched.

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:47.025
I think we're pretty good.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:48.060
I'm elated.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.094
It's straight.

00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:52.765
So I'm feeling great right now.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.467
So I'm gonna to take
the black walnut.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:55.801
I'm gonna start working it up.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:59.105
We've got to get this
hourglass design into it.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.541
We're gonna put a butt
cap on or a pommel cap.

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:04.310
And then, we're gonna
weld it and attach

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:07.880
it up so that it'll be strong
and tight and ready to go.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:12.752
I want the end of my handle to
be protected as much as I can.

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:16.822
I've got everything
all together.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:20.627
So now, just comes, really,
working on that edge

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.561
as much as I can.

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:26.766 line:8%
I feel a tremendous weight
lifted off of my shoulders.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.903
RICARDO: My name
is Ricardo Vilar.

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.038 line:14%
I'm originally from Brazil.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.641 line:8%
I immigrated to
US two years ago.

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:37.977
In Brazil, people know
about me and my knives.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:40.613
But in America, nobody knows me.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:44.283
If I do well in this
competition, people in America

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:47.052
are probably gonna
know my name too.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:49.321
I'm using water
on the anvil, just

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:51.757
to make the tip a little cooler.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:54.593
This is a very old technique
to give me the control

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:57.096
to make the shoulders better.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.197
The tip is done.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:00.433
Time to get into the oil.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.738
That's hard.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.373
I have a blade that's
good to turn in.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.276
But I think I can do better.

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:13.813
So let's turn on the
forge and start over.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:17.450
I love so much this job
that I'm making twice.

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:25.958
What took me hours before has
just took me minutes this time.

00:05:26.024 --> 00:05:27.626
And now, I'm done.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.496
I love when a plan
comes together.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.332
I quench the second blade.

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:37.770
The blade is straight.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.938
It's hard.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.407
And I'm much more confident
in the second product.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:45.277
So the second one is the
one I'm gonna compete with.

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:46.879
What I did different
in this blade

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:50.116
is it has a different edge
geometry and a harder taper.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.521
Everything is coming together.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:59.359
Now, it's time to go and see
how does it gonna perform?

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.000
For me, it's OK.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:09.902
I'm happy.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:10.837
All right, bladesmiths.

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:12.938
Welcome to the kill test.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:17.576
Well, your ikakalakas look
interesting and exotic.

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:19.712
But what kind of lethal
damage can they do?

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.514
Well, to find that out,
I'm gonna take your weapon,

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:25.384
deliver some lethal blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.986
Ricardo, you're up first.
You ready?

00:06:27.052 --> 00:06:27.953
Yes, sir.
I'm ready.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.055
Let's go for it.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:35.128
[rock music]

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:03.322
All right, Ricardo, I
like-a your ikakalaka.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.390
Thank you.

00:07:04.456 --> 00:07:06.159
It's got a good weight to it.

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:08.727
The handle construction
is comfortable.

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:10.963
When you're swinging
this, it digs deep.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:12.832
That is a sharp edge.

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:15.167
And when you're
penetrating, it really

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:17.937
digs and cuts on the way out.

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:21.006
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:22.474
Thank you, sir.

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:24.243
All right, Nick, your turn.
So are you ready?

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:25.277
I'm ready.

00:07:25.343 --> 00:07:27.546
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:07:27.646 --> 00:07:30.616 line:8%
Ricardo's ikakalaka is
everything I expected, light,

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:32.351 line:14%
fast, a well-made weapon.

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.920
But my confidence
level is pretty good.

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:37.957
I'm fairly confident that
my blade will succeed.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.799
The minute you
pick up this weapon,

00:07:47.899 --> 00:07:50.536
I feel the stress on my wrist,
my elbows, and my shoulder.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:53.171
It's so forward heavy.

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:54.406
Tell me what you feel.

00:07:54.506 --> 00:07:56.408
Front of the shoulder.

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:58.211
I'm trying to swing
this over and over.

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.479
It's gonna be tough.

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:03.115
It's not looking good.

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:10.756
Nick, due to the extreme
weight of your ikakalaka,

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:14.259
the judges feel that it would
be unsafe to attempt to wield it

00:08:14.359 --> 00:08:16.294
in the same manner
that they wielded

00:08:16.361 --> 00:08:18.163
Ricardo's one-handed blade.

00:08:18.263 --> 00:08:21.634
And because we can't test it
evenly and fairly, we cannot

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:22.868
move forward with testing.

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:24.737
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:30.142
shake your competitor's hand,
and then please exit the Forge.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:32.278
Just totally disappointed.

00:08:32.344 --> 00:08:33.612
Sorry about that.

00:08:33.712 --> 00:08:35.313
NICK: I wanted them to
really test that weapon.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:36.715
I had a lot of faith in it.

00:08:36.815 --> 00:08:40.353
I knew it was heavy, but
one little mistake like this

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.655
is something I'm gonna
learn on and build.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.190
And it's gonna make
me a better smith.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:48.994
Well, Ricardo,
congratulations.

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:51.263
You are the new Forged
in Fire Champion.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:56.068
And that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:58.370
Come on forward.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.505
Good job.

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:01.240
It's a great weapon.

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:02.241
This is great.

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:03.676
This is amazing.

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:07.446
Being the champion is you
can trust what I'm doing.

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:08.681
You can trust on my blades.

00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:10.649
You can trust on my work.

00:09:10.715 --> 00:09:13.519
I'm really, really happy
to be the champion.

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:16.822
[music playing]

